  "worked_solution": "Multiplying both sides of the given equality by $(x+2)^{3}$ gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{2}-x+4 & =A(x+2)^{2}+B(x+2)+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nLetting $x=-2$  gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(-2)^{2}-(-2)+4 & =A(-2+2)^{2}+B(-2+2)+C \\\\ 10 & =A(0)+B(0)+C \\\\ C & =10.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nLetting $x=0$ and using our value for $C$ gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(0)^{2}-(0)+4 & =A(0+2)^{2}+B(0+2)+10 \\\\ 4 & =4A+2B+10 \\\\ 0 & =4A+2B+6 \\\\ 0 & =2A+B+3 \\\\ B & =-2A-3.\\,\\,(1)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, letting $x=-1$ and using our value for $C$ gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(-1)^{2}-(-1)+4 & =A(-1+2)^{2}+B(-1+2)+10 \\\\ 6 & =A+B+10 \\\\ 0 & =A+B+4 \\\\ B & =-4-A.\\,\\,(2)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom $(1)$ and $(2)$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-2A-3 & =-4-A \\\\ -A & =-1 \\\\ A & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow we substitute the value of $A$ into $(2)$  to get the value of $B:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}B & =-4-1=-5\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A\\cdot B+C & =1\\cdot (-5)+10 \\\\  & =-5+10 \\\\  & =5.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
